Nina's Circadian Clockwork (NCC) project
========================================
Background
-------
The circadian clock is a fundamental regulator of cellular homeostasis, and its 
disruption has been implicated in aggressive neuroblastoma, particularly in 
tumours harbouring MYCN-gene amplification. 

We estimated and compared the circadian gene network dysregulation in tumours 
of patients obtained from two different cohorts (SEQC n=498 and Kocak n=649), 
with contrasting clinical features of outcome (e.g. risk, stage, and MYCN 
amplification), using as proxy the difference of the Clock correlation distance 
(Delta-CCD) with canonical, adrenal tissue matched, and developmental references.
The robustness of the results was further assessed using a meta-analysis across
the two cohorts, and leave-one-gene-out analyses. Further, Cox proportional
hazards regression models adjusted for clinical covariates were used to estimate
the association between the expression of each clock gene and patient outcome.


Purpose
-------
This project contains the input data, manifests, scripts, and results used for
NCC/CCD, Delta-CCD, matched-background, leave-one-gene-out, and Cox survival
analyses of circadian clock gene coordination.

The project is organized into the following main folders:

    data.d/
    manifest.d/
    results.d/
    results_cmbt.d/
    scripts.d/


data.d/
-------
Purpose:

    Stores input expression matrices, clinical metadata, orthology files,
    reference datasets, and other source data required by the analysis
    workflows.



manifest.d/
-----------
Purpose:

    Stores manifest files that describe reference and target datasets for the
    NCC/CCD workflows.

Manifest files tell the analysis scripts where input expression data are
located and how samples or groups should be selected.


results.d/
----------
Purpose:

    Stores analysis outputs generated from the primary expression data,
    typically the standard log2-normalized condition.


results_cmbt.d/
---------------
Purpose:

    Stores analysis outputs generated from MYCN-ComBat-corrected expression
    data.

This directory should mirror the structure of results.d/ as closely as
possible so that primary and MYCN-corrected sensitivity analyses can be
compared directly.


Important interpretation:

    results.d/
        Primary log2-expression analyses.

    results_cmbt.d/
        MYCN-ComBat-corrected technical sensitivity analyses.

The corrected analyses should generally be treated as sensitivity analyses
rather than replacements for the primary log2 analyses.


scripts.d/
----------
Purpose:

    Stores the Python and Bash scripts used to run the analysis workflows.


Suggested workflow
------------------
A typical analysis proceeds as follows:
    1. Place source data and mapping files in:
           data.d/
    2. Prepare reference and target manifests in:
           manifest.d/
    3. Run scripts from:
           scripts.d/
    4. Write primary log2 analysis outputs to:
           results.d/
    5. Write MYCN-ComBat-corrected sensitivity outputs to:
           results_cmbt.d/


Naming standards
----------------------
Reference correlation files:
    <reference_name>_<gene_set>.full_rho.tsv
    <reference_name>_<gene_set>.weighted_rho.csv

Target CCD files:
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.target_full_rho.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.background.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.CCD.tsv


Direct Delta-CCD files:
    target_clock_all_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.<contrast>.delta.tsv
    target_clock_all_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.<contrast>.delta_draws.tsv


Matched-background files:
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.target_full_rho.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.background.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.CCD.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.gene_summary.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.gene_sets.tsv


Path convention
---------------
Where possible, scripts should use variables such as:
    DATA_DIR="data.d"
    MANIFEST_DIR="manifest.d"
    RESULTS_DIR="results.d"/"results_cmbt.d"
    SCRIPTS_DIR="scripts.d"

This keeps path handling consistent across Bash workflows.


Summary
-------
    data.d/
        Raw or processed input data and mappings.
    manifest.d/
        Reference and target dataset manifests.
    results.d/
        Primary log2 NCC/CCD, Delta-CCD, LOO, Cox, and related outputs.
    results_cmbt.d/
        MYCN-ComBat-corrected sensitivity-analysis outputs.
    scripts.d/
        Python and Bash scripts used to generate all analyses.
